 "root_cause": "Permissive JSON loading accepted duplicate keys, alternate encodings, bool/float version1, bool zero subtitle anchors and non-UTF8-encodable strings. Huge integers escaped float conversion as OverflowError. Stored lone-surrogate text produced HTTP500 instead of a public artifact error.",
 "changes": [
  "Bound transcript bytes before UTF8/JSON decoding, using strict duplicate/nonfinite/overflow hooks and a recursion error boundary",
  "Require exact integer version1, numeric subtitle zero anchors and a <=16-character UTF8-encodable language",
  "Reject lone-surrogate transcript text before publication or response serialization",
  "Convert oversized/nonfinite ASR/frame timestamps to existing422 BusinessError codes",
  "Preserve valid payloads and all existing character/segment/frame/processing budgets"
 ],
